{"_id":"dDh42FZ6oY6X4ThZ","name":"Once any amount of mana is released, all stored mana will be lost. Stored Mana Damage","type":"armour","system":{"equipped":false,"evasion":2,"defence":2,"description":"3 8 4 16 If the wielder misses with the sword during their turn, or if the target does not have MP or already has 0 MP, all mana reserves are extinguished at the end of the turn (it is possible to release mana before the end of the turn). The mana stored in this shield may not be used for any purpose other than the effect of this shield. > Return to list Mighty Brittle This is a large shield produced in the Magitech Civilization Period, but contains a curse due to a flaw in the process. Due to the limited conditions of potential danger, many of them were manufactured and distributed before they were discovered. Therefore, many of them are still found in ruins. This shield has a curse with success value 15, and the character must perform a Willpower check the first time they equip this shield. If the character fails, they will not be able to equip any other shields. Even if the character succeeds in resisting once, they must perform the same check every time they equip this shield. When an Evasion check is failed with an automatic failure while this shield is equipped, the character's Defense is set to 0 and damage must be applied without Defense (all Defense and its bonuses due to armor, combat feats, magic, etc. are ignored). When this effect occurs, the shield is destroyed and the curse is automatically removed. This effect occurs even if the wearer is not cursed by the shield. This effect cannot be prevented by using a Safety Helmet. A person equipped with this shield will automatically know the effect of this shield without Appraise check. > Return to list Mirror Shield The surface of this shield is polished enough to be used as a mirror. If a character equips or holds this shield, they are considered to be holding a mirror in their hand during combat. > Return to list Spiked Shield This shield can be wielded as a weapon with stance 1H. Even if the wielder doesn't know the combat feat [Dual Wielding], the wielder can make one attack at a time with the weapon in the other hand. In this case, there is no penalty for Accuracy checks for attacks made with weapons in the other hand. Meanwhile, if the wielder has acquired the combat feat [Dual Technique], the -2 penalty to the Accuracy check will be removed when the wielder uses it as a weapon. If used in an attack, the shield's Defense is set to 0 until the beginning of the next turn (though the increased Defense due to [Armor Proficiency/Shields] will not be lost). > Return to list Temsgard's Light Dock Temsgard's Heavy Dock Temsgard's Docks are shields to be used with Temsgard's Chains, linking the chain of the weapon to the Magitech structure of the shield. The Magitech structure winds up the chain, dramatically improving the usability of the weapon. These weapons and shields can be linked in any combination. The linking and unlinking is done with a Major Action. The following effects will appear when they are linked. When used in a Thrown Attack, the combat feat [Throwing II] and other range extensions can no longer be used, and the range is always fixed at \"Range: 1(10m)\". By consuming 5 points of MP, the wielder can use a Minor Action to re-equip Temsgard's Chain. Shields can be equipped with an Effect Cartridge or Mana Cartridge. Of course, it is also possible to reload a weapon with a Major Action without expending MP. It is no longer possible to drop only one of the weapon or shield (except for re-equipping a weapon after an attack), the weapon and shield are considered a \"Stance: 2H\" item together. However, they cannot be stored in a Weapon Holder. They can only be stored in a Modified Weapon Holder, using both of its two slots. > Return to list Reflector Shield The effect of this shield occurs when the target is actually the target of the effect and is hit by it. The reflection does not occur when the wielder evades the first check to see if he is affected or not (4-6 on 1d in principle), or when the wielder succeeds in the check against \"Resistance: Negates\" (e.g. a successful Evasion check against an attack of a Dragon Arrow). Also, even if the first effect originator is equipped with this shield, the effect reflected back by this effect cannot be reflected back further (so \"endless reflecting\" does not occur). > Return to list Total Reflector Like the Reflector Shield, the wielder can bounce the effect back to its originator. In addition to \"Area: Line\", this shield can also reflect back effects of \"Area: Shot\" and \"Target: 1 Character\" back to their originator. In this case, the check with 1d is performed only if the \"Area: Line\" is reflected back; otherwise, the effect is automatically given to the effect originator. As with the Reflector Shield, the reflection occurs only when the effect is actually applied. \"Endless reflecting\" also does not occur. > Return to list Cymbal Shield This item can be used as a percussion instrument while equipped as a shield. However, it is unsuitable for playing the melody and takes a -4 penalty on Performance checks. If the wielder succeeds on an Evasion Check while this shield is equipped, it generates 1⮭ Rhythm. Also, if the wielder takes any physical damage while equipped with this (including cases where the applied damage is \"0\"), the shield generates 1⮯ Rhythm. > Return to list","magicalDefence":0,"quantity":1,"minStrength":1,"notes":"3 8 4 16 If the wielder misses with the sword during their turn, or if the target does not have MP or already has 0 MP, all mana reserves are extinguished at the end of the turn (it is possible to release mana before the end of the turn). The mana stored in this shield may not be used for any purpose other than the effect of this shield. > Return to list Mighty Brittle This is a large shield produced in the Magitech Civilization Period, but contains a curse due to a flaw in the process. Due to the limited conditions of potential danger, many of them were manufactured and distributed before they were discovered. Therefore, many of them are still found in ruins. This shield has a curse with success value 15, and the character must perform a Willpower check the first time they equip this shield. If the character fails, they will not be able to equip any other shields. Even if the character succeeds in resisting once, they must perform the same check every time they equip this shield. When an Evasion check is failed with an automatic failure while this shield is equipped, the character's Defense is set to 0 and damage must be applied without Defense (all Defense and its bonuses due to armor, combat feats, magic, etc. are ignored). When this effect occurs, the shield is destroyed and the curse is automatically removed. This effect occurs even if the wearer is not cursed by the shield. This effect cannot be prevented by using a Safety Helmet. A person equipped with this shield will automatically know the effect of this shield without Appraise check. > Return to list Mirror Shield The surface of this shield is polished enough to be used as a mirror. If a character equips or holds this shield, they are considered to be holding a mirror in their hand during combat. > Return to list Spiked Shield This shield can be wielded as a weapon with stance 1H. Even if the wielder doesn't know the combat feat [Dual Wielding], the wielder can make one attack at a time with the weapon in the other hand. In this case, there is no penalty for Accuracy checks for attacks made with weapons in the other hand. Meanwhile, if the wielder has acquired the combat feat [Dual Technique], the -2 penalty to the Accuracy check will be removed when the wielder uses it as a weapon. If used in an attack, the shield's Defense is set to 0 until the beginning of the next turn (though the increased Defense due to [Armor Proficiency/Shields] will not be lost). > Return to list Temsgard's Light Dock Temsgard's Heavy Dock Temsgard's Docks are shields to be used with Temsgard's Chains, linking the chain of the weapon to the Magitech structure of the shield. The Magitech structure winds up the chain, dramatically improving the usability of the weapon. These weapons and shields can be linked in any combination. The linking and unlinking is done with a Major Action. The following effects will appear when they are linked. When used in a Thrown Attack, the combat feat [Throwing II] and other range extensions can no longer be used, and the range is always fixed at \"Range: 1(10m)\". By consuming 5 points of MP, the wielder can use a Minor Action to re-equip Temsgard's Chain. Shields can be equipped with an Effect Cartridge or Mana Cartridge. Of course, it is also possible to reload a weapon with a Major Action without expending MP. It is no longer possible to drop only one of the weapon or shield (except for re-equipping a weapon after an attack), the weapon and shield are considered a \"Stance: 2H\" item together. However, they cannot be stored in a Weapon Holder. They can only be stored in a Modified Weapon Holder, using both of its two slots. > Return to list Reflector Shield The effect of this shield occurs when the target is actually the target of the effect and is hit by it. The reflection does not occur when the wielder evades the first check to see if he is affected or not (4-6 on 1d in principle), or when the wielder succeeds in the check against \"Resistance: Negates\" (e.g. a successful Evasion check against an attack of a Dragon Arrow). Also, even if the first effect originator is equipped with this shield, the effect reflected back by this effect cannot be reflected back further (so \"endless reflecting\" does not occur). > Return to list Total Reflector Like the Reflector Shield, the wielder can bounce the effect back to its originator. In addition to \"Area: Line\", this shield can also reflect back effects of \"Area: Shot\" and \"Target: 1 Character\" back to their originator. In this case, the check with 1d is performed only if the \"Area: Line\" is reflected back; otherwise, the effect is automatically given to the effect originator. As with the Reflector Shield, the reflection occurs only when the effect is actually applied. \"Endless reflecting\" also does not occur. > Return to list Cymbal Shield This item can be used as a percussion instrument while equipped as a shield. However, it is unsuitable for playing the melody and takes a -4 penalty on Performance checks. If the wielder succeeds on an Evasion Check while this shield is equipped, it generates 1⮭ Rhythm. Also, if the wielder takes any physical damage while equipped with this (including cases where the applied damage is \"0\"), the shield generates 1⮯ Rhythm. > Return to list","sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/items:shields","racialGearRace":""},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","effects":[],"sort":0}
